            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with nausea and epigastric pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A3071</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 48-year old woman presented at the emergency room with epigastric pain and nausea. 6 months earlier she had a distended ascending colon, which resolved quickly after conservative treatment with nasogastric tube. Now she had similar complaints. A plain abdominal radiograph was not conclusive; barium enema examination demonstrated a cecal volvulus. Patient required right hemicolectomy. She recovered uneventfully.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
